## 3. chunk.c - Implement writeConstant()

This function adds the constant to the constant pool and chooses which instruction to write based on the constant's index.

```c
void writeConstant(Chunk* chunk, Value value, int line) {
  // A 24-bit operand supports indices up to 0xFFFFFF.
  // Check before adding another constant.
  if (chunk->constants.count > 0xFFFFFF) {
    fprintf(stderr, "Too many constants in chunk.\n");
    exit(1);
  }

  int index = addConstant(chunk, value);

  // Use the short instruction if the index fits in one byte.
  if (index < 256) {
    writeChunk(chunk, OP_CONSTANT, line);
    writeChunk(chunk, (uint8_t)index, line);
  } else {
    // Use the long instruction for larger indices.
    writeChunk(chunk, OP_CONSTANT_LONG, line);

    // Store the 24-bit index in little-endian order.
    writeChunk(chunk, (uint8_t)(index & 0xff), line);
    writeChunk(chunk, (uint8_t)((index >> 8) & 0xff), line);
    writeChunk(chunk, (uint8_t)((index >> 16) & 0xff), line);
  }
}
```

This implementation requires stdio.h and stdlib.h in chunk.c for fprintf(), stderr, and exit().

