## 4. debug.c - Add longConstantInstruction()

I added a helper function to decode and display OP_CONSTANT_LONG instructions.

```c
static int longConstantInstruction(const char* name,
                                   Chunk* chunk,
                                   int offset) {
  uint32_t constant =
      (uint32_t)chunk->code[offset + 1] |
      ((uint32_t)chunk->code[offset + 2] << 8) |
      ((uint32_t)chunk->code[offset + 3] << 16);

  printf("%-16s %4u '", name, (unsigned int)constant);

  printValue(chunk->constants.values[constant]);

  printf("'\n");

  return offset + 4;
}
```

The function reads the three-byte constant index, combines the bytes into one number, and uses that index to locate the stored constant.

It returns offset + 4 because the instruction occupies four bytes total: one opcode and three operand bytes.

