## 6. vm.c - Read a Long Constant

To make the new instruction executable in the Chapter 15 virtual machine, I added a helper macro inside run().

```c
#define READ_LONG() \
  ((uint32_t)READ_BYTE() | \
   ((uint32_t)READ_BYTE() << 8) | \
   ((uint32_t)READ_BYTE() << 16))

#define READ_LONG_CONSTANT() \
  (vm.chunk->constants.values[READ_LONG()])
```

READ_LONG() combines three bytes into a 24-bit index using the same little-endian ordering used when writing the instruction.

READ_LONG_CONSTANT() uses that index to retrieve the value from the chunk's constant pool.

---

## 7. vm.c - Execute OP_CONSTANT_LONG

I added the following case to the instruction switch statement inside run().

```c
case OP_CONSTANT_LONG: {
  Value constant = READ_LONG_CONSTANT();
  push(constant);
  break;
}
```

This loads the selected constant onto the VM stack, just like the original OP_CONSTANT instruction.

At the end of run(), I also added:

```c
#undef READ_LONG
#undef READ_LONG_CONSTANT
```

